Diagnostic: fling velocity estimation tracing (WEBKIT_FLINGVEL_LOG=1, off by default).

Scroll momentum is not harmonized across sites: on some pages a flick coasts
almost not at all, on others it launches far too fast. Same gesture, same
WEBKIT_KINETIC_DECEL_FRICTION - so the variable is the *initial velocity*, not
the decay.

Suspected chain (read from source, to be confirmed on device by this patch):

  1. TouchGestureController synthesizes axis/wheel events from touch motion and
     stamps every motion event of a gesture with the touch-DOWN position
     (m_start.x, m_start.y), so WebWheelEventCoalescer::canCoalesce()'s
     position equality test always passes within one flick. The phase test that
     would otherwise block coalescing is #if PLATFORM(COCOA) only.
  2. WebWheelEventCoalescer coalesces only while m_eventsBeingProcessed is
     non-empty - i.e. exactly when the WebProcess main thread is slow to ack,
     which is a property of the page's JS/style/layout load.
  3. coalesce() merges the deltas but keeps only b.timestamp(), so the merged
     event carries the full delta over a collapsed time span.
  4. ScrollAnimationKinetic::computeVelocity() divides the summed delta by
     (last - first) over the surviving history. Fewer surviving samples =>
     same numerator, smaller denominator => inflated velocity; and at exactly
     one surviving sample last == first and it returns {0,0}: no momentum.

  It also sums N deltas but divides by the N-1 intervals between them, a
  N/(N-1) inflation that is +9% at 12 samples and +100% at 2.

This logs, per gesture: the coalescer's collapse ratio (UIProcess) and the
history sample count, time span, accumulated delta and resulting velocity
(WebProcess). Confirming the chain means seeing samples/span shrink while
accumDelta stays constant, with velocity tracking the shrink.

TEMPORARY - remove once fling velocity estimation is made coalescing-invariant.
Must apply AFTER webkit-kinetic-decel-friction-env.patch and
webkit-kinetic-jank-resilient-end.patch (same file, different hunks).

